{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/admin_setting_keycolour

    The control of an event type's colour setting: a swatch and a hexadecimal field.

    The server draws all of it; amd/src/keycolour.js only keeps the swatch and the native colour input in step with
    the field. The native input has no name, so only the text field is submitted, and without JavaScript the field
    works alone.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - the text field's id
    * name - the text field's name
    * value - what is stored, as typed
    * hex - the stored value as #rrggbb, or an empty string when it is not a hex colour
    * label - the accessible name of the native colour input
    * readonly - bool

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": "id_s_theme_dimensions_calendarcolourcourse",
        "name": "s_theme_dimensions_calendarcolourcourse",
        "value": "#2a31c9",
        "hex": "#2a31c9",
        "label": "Pick a colour",
        "readonly": false
    }
}}
<div class="dim-keycolour" data-dim-keycolour>
    <label class="dim-keycolour__swatch">
        <span class="dim-keycolour__preview{{^hex}} dim-keycolour__preview--empty{{/hex}}"{{#hex}} style="background-color: {{hex}};"{{/hex}}></span>
        <input type="color" class="dim-keycolour__native" value="{{#hex}}{{hex}}{{/hex}}{{^hex}}#000000{{/hex}}" aria-label="{{label}}" tabindex="-1"{{#readonly}} disabled{{/readonly}}>
    </label>
    <input type="text" name="{{name}}" id="{{id}}" value="{{value}}" size="12" class="form-control text-ltr dim-keycolour__field" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"{{#readonly}} disabled{{/readonly}}>
</div>
